The options flow handler never runs `iCloud3_ConfigFlow.__init__`, so
`self.AppleAcct` only exists once a login has succeeded; the error paths that
read it raise AttributeError instead of reporting the login failure.

Upstream fixed this in 3.8.0-beta.2 by initialising the attribute in the options
flow, see
https://github.com/gcobb321/icloud3/commit/5579a84511bd2420afc495a6ea21a8864eeb1780
This patch can be dropped once the package ships 3.8.0 or newer.

--- a/custom_components/icloud3/configure/screens/step_apple_acct.py
+++ b/custom_components/icloud3/configure/screens/step_apple_acct.py
@@ -39,6 +39,10 @@
 #<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
 
 class OptionsFlow_AppleAccount_Steps:
+    # `iCloud3_OptionsFlowHandler` never runs `iCloud3_ConfigFlow.__init__`, so
+    # `self.AppleAcct` does not exist until a login succeeds and the error paths
+    # that read it raise AttributeError.
+    AppleAcct = None
 
 
 #<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
